CORE
main.ii
--arch arm64 --os linux
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* unsigned: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* value: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* literal: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The procedure call standard for 64-bit Arm (AAPCS64) makes wchar_t, a keyword
of C++, an unsigned 32-bit type.
